The FastAPI backend exposes a directive `@resolve_as_url` which fetches remote content via Python’s `requests.get(resolver.url)`. Attacker crafts introspection query:

```
query {
  fetchRemoteImage(url: "http://metadata.google.internal/0.1/metadata/instance") {
    data
  }
}
```

This triggers resolver that uses the directive to resolve the URL. SSRF is confirmed via HTTP 200 OK and instance metadata returned (`project-id`, `zone`). Escalate to RCE by chaining with `@resolve_as_template` directive that uses `jinja2.Template(url)`, injecting attacker-controlled `url=http://internal:8080/?cmd={{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}}`. The backend compiles the template server-side, achieving RCE. Real-world: CVE-2023-40593 in a Kubernetes operator used similar Jinja2 template injection. Mitigation: disable GraphQL introspection in production (`/graphql?query={__schema{types{name}}}`), enforce allow-list for resolver URLs via `requests.utils.requote_uri`, and sandbox Jinja2 using `jinja2.StrictUndefined` with a custom `Environment(autoescape=True, trim_blocks=True)`.

